Z||000000||overlord||11-17-2000||10:51 PM||||was wondering if the cold is hard on stereo equipment (i.e. subs)?<BR>It is starting to get colder here now....last night was -20 C, does it hurt speakers if they are cold?<BR>Usually heat is electronics enemy, so i am a little confused if cold is bad.||||reg||1
Z||000001||goldfinger||11-18-2000||01:24 AM||||Nope, they are designed for cold, if its indoor stuff you might have a problem. But for about 5 minutes in the morning run your subs at low volumes to "warm" them up. If your headunit skips a lot its because the rubber piece that keeps it frome skipping is frozen. Thats fine just keep it playing it will go away.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||overlord||11-18-2000||08:50 AM||||excellent! and THANX||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||11-18-2000||09:25 AM||||Yep, just what he said. Warm the speakers up at a reasonable volum before cranking it up and you will be fine.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||olympic||11-19-2000||02:17 AM||||My Alpine 7817 cd player will not play when the temp is anywhewre near freezing.  Its about 8 years old and it would play at almost any temp  before.  I had the lazer cleaned and realigned but it didn't help.  Is there something that needs lubrication inside?  I can hear the laser moving but it sounds like it just cant find what its looking for.  Once the car is warmed up for a while the deck works fine.  Any ideas??||||reg||1
Z||000005||Xtreme Fiero's||11-19-2000||10:52 PM||||Alpine cd players ALL skip badly in the cold (not counting the new DVD players and CD changers) if your alpind has a "pause" butto(not all do pause a cd that will keep the cd spining and will warm up the cd player amps subs and speakers will work better in the cold amps stay cooler and speakers have more air thay can move. ||||reg||1
